// ERROR-GOL-017 (GoL/HALLAZGOS.md) — a loop that writes a visible name with a
// value of another type is the change `m = 5` warns about after `m = "fuera"`.
//
// The loop writes the outer `m` (PREMISES.md MEM-7), so after it `m` holds the
// last element. The analyser saw a second `m` in the loop and compared nothing:
// a plain reassignment warned and this one did not. Each loop below changes
// the type of a variable the program reads afterwards, so each one warns, and
// none of them warns `unused variable`.

m = "fuera"
@ m:[1, 2] {
    >> m ¶
}
>> m ¶

t = 1
@ t:"ab" {
    >> t ¶
}
>> t ¶

r = "x"
@ r:1..2 {
    >> r ¶
}
>> r ¶
